-- Module import (issue #17, §13.13): greeter is loaded at runtime
-- from greeter.lind (modules are searched in the main file's
-- directory), with namespace suffix "_v2" — every atom in the
-- module's source is suffixed, so we trigger Greet_v2 and match its
-- (Hello_v2, who) reply. The suffix is data: a bytestring handle
-- whose contents the import effect reads (Nil → "" is preregistered,
-- so `import H Nil []` spells "no suffix" — allowed, but a bad idea:
-- no namespacing). The (Imported, H, suffix) completion tuple into
-- Global is the deterministic gate, same idiom as (Bytes, H).
--
-- The module's reply lands in whatever bag we pass as data (Outbox):
-- a module can't name the real Global — its atom mentions are
-- mangled — so the caller shapes what happens next (§4).

-- Two §1 one-shots bind the module name and suffix as bytestrings;
-- their (Bytes, H) completions gate the import.
: bytesBind Greeter "greeter"
: bytesBind Suffix "_v2"

{ (Start,) }

(Bytes, Greeter), (Bytes, Suffix), (Start,) : import Greeter Suffix []

(Imported, Greeter, "_v2") : (Greet_v2, "world", Outbox)

Outbox {
  (Hello_v2, who) : [say "greeter says: hello, %s" who; exit 0]
}
